termios.h: struct winsize has four members, because the kernel sends
four.

TIOCGWINSZ is answered by copying the kernel's struct winsize to the
caller's pointer. This system's kernel uses Linux's, which is eight
bytes: rows, columns, and the two pixel dimensions a graphical terminal
fills in. picolibc declares the first two and nothing else, so every
program that asked how big its terminal was got four bytes written past
the end of its structure.

It had not been noticed because the overrun lands on whatever the
compiler happened to put next and the values are normally zero. It is
still four bytes of somebody else's memory, on every call, from every
program that asks -- which on this machine includes less, resize and
everything built on ncurses.

Found because Dropbear sets ws_xpixel by name and would not compile.

--- a/libc/include/sys/termios.h
+++ b/libc/include/sys/termios.h
@@ -73,9 +73,30 @@
     speed_t  c_ospeed;
 };
 
+/*
+ * FOUR FIELDS, NOT TWO, and this is a correctness fix rather than a
+ * feature. TIOCGWINSZ is answered by the kernel with a structure of
+ * its own, and this system's -- Linux's -- has all four: rows,
+ * columns, and the pixel dimensions that a graphical terminal fills
+ * in. The kernel copies sizeof(struct winsize) bytes to the pointer
+ * it is given, which is eight; a program whose struct was this one
+ * offered four, and the other four went past the end of it.
+ *
+ * Nothing had noticed, because the overrun lands on whatever the
+ * compiler put next on the stack and the values written are usually
+ * zero. It is still four bytes of somebody else's memory, on every
+ * call, from every program that asks how big its terminal is.
+ *
+ * ws_xpixel and ws_ypixel are zero here: this machine's terminals are
+ * a serial line and a character console, and neither has a pixel size
+ * to report. They are carried because the kernel sends them and
+ * because software reads them.
+ */
 struct winsize {
     unsigned short ws_row;
     unsigned short ws_col;
+    unsigned short ws_xpixel;
+    unsigned short ws_ypixel;
 };
 
 #define BRKINT    0x0001
